    "data": {
      "text": "===================================================================\nReport ID.....................report01_PRG\nPatient ID....................PT001234\nPatient Name..................Sample Patient A\nPrincipal Date................20231115 0930\nRecord Type...................ONCOLOGY PROGRESS NOTE\n===================================================================\n[Report de-identified (Limited dataset compliant) by De-ID v.6.24.5.1]\n\nCHIEF COMPLAINT::\nFollow-up visit for ongoing breast cancer treatment.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS::\nThe patient is a 52-year-old female with stage II invasive ductal carcinoma \nof the left breast, ER+/PR+/HER2-. She was diagnosed on June 15, 2023 via \ncore needle biopsy. Initial staging workup showed a 3.2 cm primary tumor \nwith one positive axillary lymph node.\n\nTREATMENT COURSE::\nThe patient initiated neoadjuvant chemotherapy on July 10, 2023.\nShe completed 4 cycles of Doxorubicin (Adriamycin) and\nCyclophosphamide every 3 weeks, with the last dose administered on \nSeptember 18, 2023. She tolerated this phase well with manageable nausea \nand fatigue.\n\nShe then transitioned to Paclitaxel (Taxol) starting\nOctober 2, 2023. Most recent infusion was yesterday.\nShe reports mild peripheral neuropathy\nin her fingertips but states it is tolerable.\n\nThe patient also started Anastrozole 1mg daily on October 15, 2023 for \nendocrine therapy, which she will continue for 5 years post-treatment.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN::\nThe patient is responding well to neoadjuvant chemotherapy. Repeat imaging \nfrom last week shows significant reduction in tumor size to approximately \n1.5 cm. She will complete her remaining 4 weekly doses of Paclitaxel with \nthe final infusion scheduled for November 27, 2023.\n\nSigned by: Dr. Jane Smith, MD\nDate: November 15, 2023 at 10:15 AM\n"
    },
