      "text": "===================================================================\nReport ID.....................report01_PRG\nPatient ID....................PT003456\nPatient Name..................Sample Patient C\nPrincipal Date................20240215 1030\nRecord Type...................ONCOLOGY PROGRESS NOTE\n===================================================================\n[Report de-identified (Limited dataset compliant) by De-ID v.6.24.5.1]\n\nCHIEF COMPLAINT::\nFollow-up for ovarian cancer treatment.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS::\nThe patient is a 61-year-old female diagnosed with stage IIIC high-grade\nserous ovarian carcinoma in November 2023. She underwent total abdominal\nhysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy and optimal debulking\nsurgery on December 5, 2023.\n\nTREATMENT HISTORY::\nPostoperatively, the patient initiated adjuvant chemotherapy with\ncarboplatin AUC 5 and paclitaxel 175 mg/m2 on January 8, 2024. She has\nnow completed 3 cycles of chemotherapy with treatments every 3 weeks.\nMost recent infusion was on February 12, 2024. She is scheduled to receive\na total of 6 cycles.\n\nThe patient tolerates chemotherapy reasonably well. She experiences fatigue\nfor 3-4 days post-infusion and some mild nausea controlled with ondansetron.\nNo significant cytopenias noted on recent labs.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION::\nVitals: BP 118/72, HR 68, Temp 98.4\\u00b0F\nGeneral: Well-appearing, no acute distress\nAbdomen: Soft, well-healed surgical incision, non-tender\nExtremities: No edema, no evidence of neuropathy\n\nLABORATORY RESULTS::\nCA-125 from last week: 42 (decreased from 156 at baseline)\nCBC: WBC 4.2, Hgb 11.8, Platelets 185 - all within acceptable range\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN::\n61-year-old female with stage IIIC ovarian cancer showing good response\nto adjuvant platinum-based chemotherapy as evidenced by declining CA-125.\n\nPlan:\n1. Continue carboplatin/paclitaxel for 3 additional cycles\n2. Next infusion scheduled for March 4, 2024 (cycle 4 of 6)\n3. Repeat CA-125 with next cycle\n4. After completion of chemotherapy, will discuss maintenance therapy options\n5. Patient counseled on managing fatigue and maintaining nutrition\n\nSigned by: Dr. Jane Smith, MD\nDate: February 15, 2024 at 11:00 AM\n"
    },
